      ],
      "text": "of IPT to the post-partum period would deprive women of its protective effect at a time when they are",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.976625442504883,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        80.59070587158203,
        527.5369262695312,
        95.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "more vulnerable to TB. Moreover, a study published in 2023 showed no difference in acquisition of TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.983187675476074,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        93.79071807861328,
        527.2317504882812,
        108.23371887207031
      ],
      "text": "in the infants of mothers with HIV who received IPT during pregnancy and those who received it post",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.994647979736328,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        105.71472930908203,
        527.3952026367188,
        121.43373107910156
      ],
      "text": "(114) partum  . Appropriate care during the antenatal and postnatal periods and during delivery may",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        120.19074249267578,
        527.4432983398438,
        134.6337432861328
      ],
      "text": "reduce the risk of adverse pregnancy outcomes. While baseline testing for liver function is strongly",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        133.39076232910156,
        527.4552612304688,
        147.83375549316406
      ],
      "text": "encouraged when IPT is given during pregnancy, it is not required, and routine liver function testing",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        146.5907745361328,
        527.4028930664062,
        161.0337677001953
      ],
      "text": "when IPT is given in pregnancy is not indicated unless other risk factors for liver toxicity are present.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        159.79078674316406,
        527.4364624023438,
        174.23377990722656
      ],
      "text": "Routine vitamin B6 supplementation should nevertheless be considered. The GDG agreed that the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        172.9907989501953,
        527.4476318359375,
        187.4337921142578
      ],
      "text": "area requires more research, such as on the pharmacokinetics of IPT, pharmacovigilance and other",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        186.19081115722656,
        527.420166015625,
        200.63380432128906
      ],
      "text": "preventive treatment regimens. Rifampicin is generally considered safe in pregnancy. There are few",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        199.3908233642578,
        527.595458984375,
        213.8338165283203
      ],
      "text": "data on the pharmacokinetics and safety of rifapentine in pregnancy, precluding use of 3HP and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        212.59083557128906,
        527.441650390625,
        227.03382873535156
      ],
      "text": "1HP in pregnancy until more information on the appropriate dosing and safety of these regimens",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        225.7907257080078,
        527.435546875,
        240.2337188720703
      ],
      "text": "becomes available. In a study of 3HP in 112 pregnant women, the rates of spontaneous abortion",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        237.71461486816406,
        527.4282836914062,
        253.43373107910156
      ],
      "text": "(97) . Moreover, the results of  and birth defects were similar to those in the general US population",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        252.1906280517578,
        527.4387817382812,
        266.6336364746094
      ],
      "text": "a recent trial in Africa showed that the frequency of spontaneous abortion and adverse pregnancy",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        265.390625,
        527.3892211914062,
        279.8336486816406
      ],
      "text": "outcomes (when analysed as a composite outcome) were similar in 63 women exposed to 3HP and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        277.3145751953125,
        303.84088134765625,
        293.0336608886719
      ],
      "text": "(115) . in 142 women who were not exposed to 3HP",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.37223052978516,
        303.4571838378906,
        261.59698486328125,
        321.7272033691406
      ],
      "text": "Other subgroups and settings",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 14.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        328.43310546875,
        527.59326171875,
        342.8761291503906
      ],
      "text": "In candidates for transplantation or anti-TNF treatment, it may be particularly important to complete",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.99744987487793,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        341.63311767578125,
        527.2301635742188,
        356.0761413574219
      ],
      "text": "TPT rapidly; therefore, shorter regimens such as 1HP and 3HP could be advantageous. Likewise,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        354.8330993652344,
        527.459228515625,
        369.276123046875
      ],
      "text": "shorter treatment could be more suitable than longer regimens for homeless people and people being",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.952848434448242,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        368.0331115722656,
        525.3927612304688,
        382.47613525390625
      ],
      "text": "released from prison, for whom there is limited opportunity for repeated encounters for treatment.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        389.7370910644531,
        527.4542236328125,
        404.18011474609375
      ],
      "text": "Other populations, in addition to people with HIV on ART, who may be more commonly at risk of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        402.9371032714844,
        527.5617065429688,
        417.380126953125
      ],
      "text": "drug–drug interactions with rifampicin, include women of childbearing age on contraceptive medicines",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.951090812683105,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        416.1371154785156,
        527.489501953125,
        430.58013916015625
      ],
      "text": "(who should be counselled about potential interactions and consider nonhormonal birth control while",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.972465515136719,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        429.33709716796875,
        430.9803771972656,
        443.7801208496094
      ],
      "text": "receiving rifampicin) and opiate users on substitution therapy with methadone.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.37223052978516,
        454.2037048339844,
        205.02017211914062,
        472.4737243652344
      ],
      "text": "Other considerations",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 14.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        479.1795959472656,
        527.3991088867188,
        493.62261962890625
      ],
      "text": "With the widespread use of rifampicin-containing fixed-dose combinations to treat drug-susceptible",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        492.3796081542969,
        527.4821166992188,
        506.8226318359375
      ],
      "text": "TB, the demand by TB programmes for single-dose rifampicin has decreased. Quality-assured supplies",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.959174156188965,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        505.57958984375,
        527.5787353515625,
        520.0225830078125
      ],
      "text": "of rifampicin should be used. Provision of 4R outside TB programme centres (e.g. primary care facilities,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.950589179992676,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        518.7796020507812,
        527.2361450195312,
        533.2225952148438
      ],
      "text": "HIV programmes) should be accompanied by stepwise guidance on maximizing the effect of rifampicin",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.948328971862793,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        531.9796142578125,
        510.9504089355469,
        546.422607421875
      ],
      "text": "and on avoiding its diversion for improper use as a broad-spectrum antibiotic in the community.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        553.6834716796875,
        527.5674438476562,
        568.12646484375
      ],
      "text": "Fixed-dose combinations of rifampicin plus isoniazid – including dispersible formulations for children –",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.964943885803223,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        566.883544921875,
        527.445556640625,
        581.3265380859375
      ],
      "text": "should be used when possible to reduce the number of pills to be taken. Combinations of 300 mg",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        580.0836181640625,
        527.39306640625,
        594.526611328125
      ],
      "text": "isoniazid with 300 mg rifapentine are now also available, which will facilitate administration of 3HP",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        592.0075073242188,
        527.4297485351562,
        607.7265014648438
      ],
      "text": "(12) to adults  . For children, dispersible formulations of both isoniazid and rifapentine can facilitate",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        606.4835205078125,
        527.5050048828125,
        620.926513671875
      ],
      "text": "administration of 3HP. Shorter regimens are also more likely to be completed. Concern about",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        619.6834716796875,
        527.4470825195312,
        634.12646484375
      ],
      "text": "adherence should not be a barrier to starting TPT, and support should be provided to ensure better",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        632.8834838867188,
        527.338623046875,
        647.3264770507812
      ],
      "text": "person-centred care. There are no data-supported recommendations on handling interruptions",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        646.0836181640625,
        527.380615234375,
        660.526611328125
      ],
      "text": "of TPT, such as on how many missed doses can be made up for by prolonging treatment without",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        659.2835083007812,
        175.0522918701172,
        673.7265014648438
      ],
      "text": "compromising efficacy.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86612701416016,
        680.9874877929688,
        527.3361206054688,
        695.4304809570312
      ],
      "text": "Individuals at risk of peripheral neuropathy, such as those with malnutrition, chronic alcohol",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86612701416016,
        694.1875,
        527.3770751953125,
        708.6304931640625
      ],
      "text": "dependence, HIV infection, renal failure or diabetes or who are pregnant or breastfeeding, should",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        707.3873901367188,
        527.2710571289062,
        721.8303833007812
      ],
      "text": "receive pyridoxine (vitamin B6) when taking isoniazid-containing regimens. A different dose of isoniazid",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.947826385498047,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        720.5875244140625,
        527.3809204101562,
        735.030517578125
      ],
      "text": "from that proposed might be required to avoid toxicity if there is a high population prevalence of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        733.7874755859375,
        527.6217651367188,
        748.23046875
      ],
      "text": "“slow acetylators”. Combination tablets of co-trimoxazole, isoniazid and pyridoxine could be given to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.997200012207031,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        746.9874877929688,
        494.9441833496094,
        761.4304809570312
      ],
      "text": "people with HIV. Lack of availability of pyridoxine should not be a reason for withholding TPT.",
